==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|ang|h₁eḱ}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*ehwaz||horse}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁éḱwos||horse}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|ehuskalk|''ehu''skalk|horse-rider}}, Old High German {{m|goh|eha-}} (in personal names), Old Norse {{m|non|jór}}, Gothic {{m|got|𐌰𐌹𐍈𐍃|tr=aihws}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{m|la|equus}}, Avestan {{m|ae||tr=aspa-}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|अश्व|sc=Deva|tr=áśva}}, Old Armenian {{m|xcl|էշ||donkey}}, Tocharian A ''[[yuk]]'' B ''[[yakwe]]'', Proto-Baltic {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*ečwā-}} (Lithuanian ''[[ašva|ašvà]]''), Old Irish ''[[ech]]'' (Irish ''[[each]]'').

